.TH BAO\-KIT 1 "2026-09-06" "NuCode" "LAN vault"
.SH NAME
bao-kit \- the personal-Vault workflow wrapper

.SH COMMANDS
.SS Setup and authentication
.TP
.BI env
Print shell exports (BAO_ADDR, BAO_CACERT, and BAO_TOKEN if a login is cached); use as: eval "$(bao-kit env)".
.TP
.BI init
One‑time setup. Initialises the vault with a single unseal key share, unseals it, enables the kv v2 secrets engine at kv/, enables userpass auth, enables the file audit device, writes the operator policy. Writes the unseal key and root token to ~/.config/openbao/init.json at mode 600.
.TP
.BI unseal
The morning ritual. The PC sleeps at night and the vault seals; this reads the stored unseal key from init.json and unseals, then prints status.
.TP
.BI user
Create or reset the ziggy operator user. Prompts for a password, so run it in a terminal. The user gets the operator policy and 12h tokens (24h max).
.TP
.BI login
Log in as ziggy. Prompts for the password, obtains a 12h operator token, and caches it in ~/.config/openbao/token.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Projects and secrets
.TP
.BI project " NAME"
Create or refresh the policy project-NAME, granting read on kv/NAME/*, and a token role project-NAME (orphan service tokens, 24h max) that mints session tokens carrying that policy.
.TP
.BI put " NAME/KEY" field=value ...
Store a secret at kv/NAME/KEY. It MERGES the given fields into an existing secret (it patches; it does not replace the whole secret), and creates the secret if absent.
.TP
.B status
Print seal state and health (sealed, initialized, version) and, if a token is loaded, who am I (display name, policies, ttl, metadata).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Sessions and delegation
.TP
.BI session " NAME \-\- CMD..."
Mint an 8h token scoped to project NAME (policy project-NAME), run CMD with BAO_TOKEN, BAO_SESSION and BAO_PROJECT set in its environment, and revoke the token when CMD exits. CMD defaults to claude. Revocation cascades to any child tokens the session minted.
.TP
.BI sub " [TTL] [USES]"
Run from inside a session. Mint a use-limited child token for a subagent. TTL defaults to 30m, USES defaults to 2.
.TP
.BI wrap " NAME/KEY [TTL]"
Print a single-use response-wrapping token that carries the secret at kv/NAME/KEY. TTL defaults to 5m. Hand the token to a subagent.
.TP
.BI unwrap " TOKEN"
The subagent side of wrap. Unwrap the token and print the secret fields as KEY=VALUE lines. This is one of the two commands that print a secret.
.TP
.BI with " NAME/KEY:field=ENV[,field=ENV] \-\- CMD..."
Read the secret at kv/NAME/KEY and run CMD with each named field placed in the child's environment as the given ENV variable. The secret is only ever in the child's environment, never printed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BI BAO_ADDR " "
the vault address. Defaults to https://192.168.88.18:8200 .
.TP
.BI BAO_CACERT " "
path to the self\-signed CA cert. Defaults to the tls/bao.crt file under the bao-kit install directory.
.TP
.BI BAO_FORMAT " "
bao-kit sets this to json internally so it can parse output. Note that with json format, bao's \-field= prints a quoted string.
.TP
.BI BAO_TOKEN " "
the auth token. If set in the environment it takes precedence over the cached token file (this is deliberate for scoped sessions, but a STALE exported BAO_TOKEN will shadow a fresh login; see NOTES).
.TP
.BI BAO_SESSION " "
set by the session command in the child environment, naming the session id.
.TP
.BI BAO_PROJECT " "
set by the session command in the child environment, naming the project.
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI ~/.config/openbao/init.json
the unseal key and root token from init, mode 600. Required by unseal.
.TP
.BI ~/.config/openbao/token
the cached operator login token, mode 600, loaded when BAO_TOKEN is unset.
.TP
.BI tls/bao.crt
the self-signed CA certificate, under the install directory.
.TP
.BI policies/operator.hcl
the operator policy, written by init.
.SH NOTES
.TP
.BI "BAO_TOKEN"
A stale BAO_TOKEN in the shell shadows a fresh login. bao-kit only loads the cached token file when BAO_TOKEN is unset, so an exported token left over from a previous session keeps being used and every call fails with a 403 even right after login. Fix: unset BAO_TOKEN before the command.
.TP
.BI "bao kv put"
put merges fields into an existing secret rather than replacing it, so adding one field does not erase the others. (A plain bao kv put would replace the whole secret.)
.TP
.BI "non-root token"
A non-root token can only mint child tokens whose policies are a subset of its own; sessions mint through the token role project-NAME created by the project command.
.TP
.BI "vault seals"
The vault seals whenever the host reboots; unseal is a daily step.
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
.BI bao(1)
the raw OpenBao CLI
.TP
.BI bao(1)
local deployment is documented in bao(1) as configured here (same box).
.TP
.BI /data/NuCode/Bao/README.md
